IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`
IMPORT `euca-s207-dates`
IMPORT `euca-s204-payments`
IMPORT `euca-s205-definitions`
IMPORT `euca-s208-sea`

-- Tests for section 204 (payments to States), section 205 (definitions) and section 208
-- (self-employment assistance). Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text before
-- the file was run; each case says what the hand calculation was. Money is in dollars.
-- Nothing here is a rule of the Act.

§ `Tests: sections 204, 205 and 208`

§§ `Fixtures for section 204`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of compensation paid`
      amount IS A NUMBER
      extendedEarlier IS A NUMBER
      regularEarlier IS A NUMBER
      eligible IS A BOOLEAN
      smallest IS A NUMBER
      weeklyAmount IS A NUMBER
      highUnemployment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Compensation paid for a week`
`in the payment tests, a payment of` kind amount extendedEarlier regularEarlier eligible smallest weeklyAmount highUnemployment MEANS
    `Compensation paid for a week` WITH
        `kind of compensation paid` IS kind
        `amount paid for the week` IS amount
        `extended compensation paid to the individual earlier in the benefit year` IS extendedEarlier
        `regular compensation paid or deemed paid to the individual for prior weeks in the benefit year` IS regularEarlier
        `the week is in the individual's eligibility period` IS eligible
        `smallest of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` IS smallest
        `average weekly benefit amount, including allowances for dependents, for weeks of total unemployment` IS weeklyAmount
        `section 202(b)(3)(A) applies to the week` IS highUnemployment
        `the State is entitled to reimbursement under a Federal law other than this title` IS FALSE
        `first week in the eligibility period for which extended compensation or sharable regular compensation is paid` IS FALSE
        `the State law provides for payment of regular compensation for a first week of otherwise compensable unemployment` IS FALSE
        `benefits are not payable for the week by reason of section 233 of the Trade Act of 1974` IS FALSE
        `amount that would be paid for the week if the State rounded down to the nearest lower full dollar` IS amount
        `base period wages attributable to services to which section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue Code applies` IS 0
        `total base period wages` IS 0

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      rounded IS A NUMBER
      reimbursed IS A BOOLEAN
      firstWeek IS A BOOLEAN
      stateFirstWeek IS A BOOLEAN
      trade IS A BOOLEAN
      serviceWages IS A NUMBER
      totalWages IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Compensation paid for a week`
`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` amount rounded reimbursed firstWeek stateFirstWeek trade serviceWages totalWages MEANS
    `Compensation paid for a week` WITH
        `kind of compensation paid` IS `extended compensation`
        `amount paid for the week` IS amount
        `extended compensation paid to the individual earlier in the benefit year` IS 0
        `regular compensation paid or deemed paid to the individual for prior weeks in the benefit year` IS 0
        `the week is in the individual's eligibility period` IS TRUE
        `smallest of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` IS 5000
        `average weekly benefit amount, including allowances for dependents, for weeks of total unemployment` IS 400
        `section 202(b)(3)(A) applies to the week` IS FALSE
        `the State is entitled to reimbursement under a Federal law other than this title` IS reimbursed
        `first week in the eligibility period for which extended compensation or sharable regular compensation is paid` IS firstWeek
        `the State law provides for payment of regular compensation for a first week of otherwise compensable unemployment` IS stateFirstWeek
        `benefits are not payable for the week by reason of section 233 of the Trade Act of 1974` IS trade
        `amount that would be paid for the week if the State rounded down to the nearest lower full dollar` IS rounded
        `base period wages attributable to services to which section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue Code applies` IS serviceWages
        `total base period wages` IS totalWages

§§ `204(b): sharable extended compensation`

-- Smallest of the three amounts 5,000; 400 paid, 4,600 paid earlier: 400 more fits (4,600 + 400 = 5,000).
#ASSERT `the sharable extended compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `extended compensation` 400 4600 0 TRUE 5000 400 FALSE) EQUALS 400
-- 4,800 earlier: only 200 fits.
#ASSERT `the sharable extended compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `extended compensation` 400 4800 0 TRUE 5000 400 FALSE) EQUALS 200
-- 5,000 earlier: the cap is reached: nothing is sharable. 5,200 earlier: nothing, not a negative sum.
#ASSERT `the sharable extended compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `extended compensation` 400 5000 0 TRUE 5000 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the sharable extended compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `extended compensation` 400 5200 0 TRUE 5000 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- A week outside the eligibility period is not sharable extended compensation.
#ASSERT `the sharable extended compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `extended compensation` 400 0 0 FALSE 5000 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- Regular compensation is not sharable extended compensation.
#ASSERT `the sharable extended compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10400 TRUE 5000 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0

§§ `204(c): sharable regular compensation`

-- Weekly benefit amount 400: the band is 26 x 400 = 10,400 to 39 x 400 = 15,600 (46 x 400 = 18,400 in a high unemployment period).
#ASSERT `the upper limit of the sharable regular compensation band` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 0 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 15600
#ASSERT `the upper limit of the sharable regular compensation band` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 0 TRUE 0 400 TRUE) EQUALS 18400
-- 10,000 paid earlier + 400 = 10,400: it does not EXCEED 26 x 400, so none of this week's payment is sharable.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10000 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- 10,200 + 400 = 10,600: 200 of it is over 10,400.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10200 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 200
-- 10,400 + 400 = 10,800: all 400 is over.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10400 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 400
-- 15,400 + 400 = 15,800: only up to 39 x 400 = 15,600 is sharable: 15,600 - 15,400 = 200.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 15400 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 200
-- The same in a high unemployment period: the band reaches 18,400: all 400.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 15400 TRUE 0 400 TRUE) EQUALS 400
-- 15,600 already paid: nothing more is in the band.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 15600 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- 9,000 + 400 = 9,400: under 10,400, nothing is sharable (not a negative sum).
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 9000 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- A week outside the eligibility period: not sharable even over the band.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10400 FALSE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- Extended compensation is not sharable regular compensation.
#ASSERT `the sharable regular compensation for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `extended compensation` 400 0 10400 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 0

§§ `204(a)(2): compensation for which no payment is made`

-- No exclusion applies: 400 is counted.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 400
-- (A) reimbursed under another Federal law: nothing counted.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- (B) the first week of the eligibility period, in a State that pays regular compensation for a first week: nothing counted.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- (B) does not apply where the State law has no such rule.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 400
-- (B) does not apply to a week that is not the first.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 400
-- (C) benefits not payable by reason of section 233 of the Trade Act of 1974.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- (D) 400.75 paid where rounding down would pay 400: only 400 is counted. 400 paid against 400: 400.
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400.75 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 400
-- (D) an amount below the rounded-down figure is counted in full (the rule only trims an excess).
#ASSERT `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 399 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 399

§§ `204(a)(1) and (3): one-half, and the reduction for services under section 3306(c)(7)`

-- 400 of sharable extended compensation: one-half is 200.
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week but for section 204(a)(3)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 200
-- Of 4,000 of base period wages, 1,000 are for services to which section 3306(c)(7) applies: the ratio is one-quarter; 200 less 50 is 150.
#ASSERT `the amount payable after the reduction in section 204(a)(3)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 4000) 200 EQUALS 150
-- All the wages are for such services: nothing is payable.
#ASSERT `the amount payable after the reduction in section 204(a)(3)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 4000 4000) 200 EQUALS 0
-- No such wages: no reduction. No wages at all: no ratio to take, no reduction.
#ASSERT `the amount payable after the reduction in section 204(a)(3)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4000) 200 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the amount payable after the reduction in section 204(a)(3)` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) 200 EQUALS 200
-- The whole: 200 less the one-quarter reduction is 150.
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week` (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 4000) EQUALS 150
-- Regular compensation in the band: 400 sharable, one-half is 200.
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10400 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 200
-- A regular payment's half-and-half: the extended part is zero, so only the regular half counts.
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week but for section 204(a)(3)` (`in the payment tests, a payment of` `regular compensation` 400 0 10400 TRUE 0 400 FALSE) EQUALS 200

§§ `207 with 204: which weeks section 204 reaches`

-- 31 December 1971 is outside section 204 unless the State's extended benefit period was set under section 207(b)(1); 1 January 1972 is inside.
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week of unemployment` (Date 31 12 1971) FALSE (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week of unemployment` (Date 31 12 1971) TRUE (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the amount payable to the State for the week of unemployment` (Date 1 1 1972) FALSE (`in the payment tests, an extended payment with` 400 400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 200

§§ `204(d), (e): monthly payment, certification and payment`

-- Estimate 100,000; earlier estimates were 3,000 too great: pay 97,000. Earlier estimates were 2,000 too small: pay 102,000.
#ASSERT `the sum to be paid to the State for the calendar month` 100000 3000 EQUALS 97000
#ASSERT `the sum to be paid to the State for the calendar month` 100000 (0 MINUS 2000) EQUALS 102000
#ASSERT `the party who certifies the sums payable to each State` EQUALS `the Secretary of Labor`
#ASSERT `the party who pays each State the certified sums` EQUALS `the Secretary of the Treasury`
#ASSERT `the sum the Secretary of the Treasury must pay the State` 97000 EQUALS 97000

§§ `Fixtures for section 205`

GIVEN cash IS A BOOLEAN
      unemployment IS A BOOLEAN
      stateLaw IS A BOOLEAN
      chapter85 IS A BOOLEAN
      exhaustees IS A BOOLEAN
      inPeriod IS A BOOLEAN
      conforming IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment to an individual`
`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` cash unemployment stateLaw chapter85 exhaustees inPeriod conforming MEANS
    `Payment to an individual` WITH
        `cash benefits` IS cash
        `payable with respect to the individual's unemployment` IS unemployment
        `payable under a State unemployment compensation law` IS stateLaw
        `payable pursuant to 5 U.S.C. chapter 85` IS chapter85
        `payable to exhaustees by reason of conditions of high unemployment or by reason of other special factors` IS exhaustees
        `for a week of unemployment beginning in an extended benefit period` IS inPeriod
        `under provisions of the State law which satisfy the requirements of this title with respect to the payment of extended compensation` IS conforming

§§ `205(1) to (4): compensation, regular, extended and additional`

#ASSERT `the payment is compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- A cash benefit under State law, in no extended benefit period, to a non-exhaustee: regular compensation, not extended or additional.
#ASSERT `the payment is regular compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is extended compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is additional compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Payable under 5 U.S.C. chapter 85 (not a State law): still regular compensation.
#ASSERT `the payment is regular compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Payable under neither a State law nor chapter 85: not regular compensation.
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is regular compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- A week in an extended benefit period, under conforming provisions: extended compensation, so not regular.
#ASSERT `the payment is extended compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is regular compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- In the period but under provisions that do not satisfy the title: not extended compensation; so regular compensation.
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is extended compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the payment is regular compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Additional compensation (to exhaustees for high unemployment): not regular compensation even outside an extended benefit period.
#ASSERT `the payment is additional compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment is regular compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- Additional compensation in an extended benefit period under conforming provisions is extended compensation too ("including additional compensation").
#ASSERT `the payment is extended compensation` (`in the payment tests, a payment to an individual of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `205(5), (6), (7), (8), (9), (10), (11)`

#ASSERT (`the benefit year under section 205(5)` (Date 1 3 2012) (Date 28 2 2013))'s `last day of the benefit year` EQUALS Date 28 2 2013
#ASSERT (`the base period under section 205(6)` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 31 12 2011))'s `first day of the base period` EQUALS Date 1 1 2011
#ASSERT `the week under section 205(11)` (Date 3 2 2013) EQUALS Date 3 2 2013
#ASSERT `the Secretary under section 205(7)` EQUALS `the Secretary of Labor`
#ASSERT `the agency is the State agency` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the agency is the State agency` FALSE)
-- State law is the law of the State approved by the Secretary under section 3304 of the Internal Revenue Code: both are needed.
#ASSERT `the law is the State law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the law is the State law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the law is the State law` FALSE TRUE)
-- State includes the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands; another place is not named.
#ASSERT `the status of the place under the definition of State` `a State of the United States` EQUALS `counts as a State for this title`
#ASSERT `the status of the place under the definition of State` `the District of Columbia` EQUALS `counts as a State for this title`
#ASSERT `the status of the place under the definition of State` `the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico` EQUALS `counts as a State for this title`
#ASSERT `the status of the place under the definition of State` `the Virgin Islands` EQUALS `counts as a State for this title`
#ASSERT `the status of the place under the definition of State` `a place the definition of State does not name` EQUALS `is not named by the definition of State, which says only what a State includes`

§§ `208(a): the State's option`

-- The date of enactment is 22 February 2012 (the OLRC's note); weeks beginning AFTER it. The day itself is not after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation may be paid as a self-employment assistance allowance for the week` (Date 22 2 2012) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `extended compensation may be paid as a self-employment assistance allowance for the week` (Date 23 2 2012) TRUE TRUE
-- No program established by the State: no allowance. An individual who would not otherwise satisfy the title's criteria: none.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation may be paid as a self-employment assistance allowance for the week` (Date 3 2 2013) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation may be paid as a self-employment assistance allowance for the week` (Date 3 2 2013) TRUE FALSE)
-- (a)(2): an allowance of 400 leaves 4,600 in an account of 5,000.
#ASSERT `the amount in the extended compensation account after the allowance is paid` 5000 400 EQUALS 4600

§§ `208(a)(3): the combined eligibility limit`

#ASSERT `the combined eligibility limit in weeks` EQUALS 26
-- 25 weeks already: one more is allowed (the 26th). 26 weeks already: no more.
#ASSERT `self-employment assistance allowances may be provided for a further week` 25
#ASSERT NOT (`self-employment assistance allowances may be provided for a further week` 26)
#ASSERT `weeks of allowances still available under the combined eligibility limit` 20 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `weeks of allowances still available under the combined eligibility limit` 30 EQUALS 0
-- (B): participating, 25 weeks when extended compensation ran out, otherwise eligible for title IV of the 2008 Act: may continue.
#ASSERT `the individual is eligible for allowances under section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 until the combined eligibility limit is reached` TRUE 25 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual is eligible for allowances under section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 until the combined eligibility limit is reached` TRUE 26 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual is eligible for allowances under section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 until the combined eligibility limit is reached` FALSE 25 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual is eligible for allowances under section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 until the combined eligibility limit is reached` TRUE 25 FALSE)

§§ `208(b): what the program is`

#ASSERT `the program is a self-employment assistance program for this section` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the program is a self-employment assistance program for this section` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the words read in place of regular unemployment compensation under the State law` EQUALS "extended compensation under title II of the Federal-State Extended Unemployment Compensation Act of 1970"
#ASSERT count `the paragraphs of the section 3306(t) definition that do not apply to a program under this section` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the percentage read in place of 5 percent in paragraph (4) of the section 3306(t) definition` EQUALS 1

§§ `208(c): the 13 times test`

-- Weekly benefit amount 400: 13 x 400 = 5,200. Expecting 5,200 is enough; 5,199 is not.
#ASSERT `the individual may receive self-employment assistance allowances under section 208(c)` 5200 400
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual may receive self-employment assistance allowances under section 208(c)` 5199 400)

§§ `208(d): electing out, and going back to extended compensation`

#ASSERT `the individual may elect to discontinue participation at any time` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual may elect to discontinue participation at any time` FALSE)
-- Participation ended and the individual still satisfies the title's requirements: payments resume, up to what remains in the account.
#ASSERT `the individual receives extended compensation payments for subsequent weeks` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual receives extended compensation payments for subsequent weeks` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual receives extended compensation payments for subsequent weeks` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the most extended compensation that may be paid for subsequent weeks` TRUE TRUE 3000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the most extended compensation that may be paid for subsequent weeks` TRUE FALSE 3000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most extended compensation that may be paid for subsequent weeks` TRUE TRUE (0 MINUS 10) EQUALS 0
